  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Using prime factorisation, find the HCF and LCM of:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$12\\,960$ and $3600$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "HCF $=720$, LCM $=64\\,800$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}12\\,960&=2^5\\times3^4\\times5\\\\3600&=2^4\\times3^2\\times5^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor the HCF, take the smaller power of each common prime. For the LCM, take the larger power of every prime present.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{HCF}&=2^4\\times3^2\\times5\\\\\\mathrm{HCF}&=720\\\\\\mathrm{LCM}&=2^5\\times3^4\\times5^2\\\\\\mathrm{LCM}&=64\\,800\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$1750$ and $1176$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "HCF $=14$, LCM $=147\\,000$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1750&=2\\times5^3\\times7\\\\1176&=2^3\\times3\\times7^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor the HCF, take the smaller power of each common prime. For the LCM, take the larger power of every prime present.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{HCF}&=2\\times7\\\\\\mathrm{HCF}&=14\\\\\\mathrm{LCM}&=2^3\\times3\\times5^3\\times7^2\\\\\\mathrm{LCM}&=147\\,000\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
